# Native Lean

Smallest diff; approved refactors exempt from churn. Rationale comments ok, no noise. `stop.sh` advises on churn (added+deleted ≥50% vs HEAD) and mass reindent; law you follow, not a block.

## Ladder
1. No code
2. Reuse (Grep)
3. Stdlib
4. Platform
5. Installed dep
6. One-liner
7. Minimum (new code: soft ~80; split before 120; hard 300; never 500. Legacy >700: modules ≤300)

## Quality
Match 1–2 siblings before Write. Named exports (framework contracts win). Early return. Nesting ≤2. No `any` / un-narrowed `unknown` / blind casts. Zero dead code. Zero redundant code (third copy → extract; two copies are cheaper).

## Tools
Read, Grep, Glob, Write, StrReplace, EditNotebook, Delete.
Shell: builds, tests, git. `before_shell.sh` denies Shell source-write.

## Split
Over roof: Write new modules, StrReplace original to imports, Grep callers. Never Shell sed.

## Procedure
Complex or architecture: **Read `~/.cursor/skills/ponytail/SKILL.md`**
